The commands listed below are used in cobbler (import_signatues.py)

scan_signature searches for:
    signature_dir
    "version_file"
 if "version_file_regex" -> use it to double check the integrity
    "default_autoinstall"

get_valid_arches searches for:
    all valid architectures and gives out all valid types (or empty list)
    "supported_arches"

get_valid_repo_breeds searches for:
    all valid repository breeds and gives out all valid types (or empty list)
    "supported_repo_breeds"

distro_adder searches for:
    matching kernel and initrd, and adds them to the list
    "kernel_file"
    "initrd_file"
    mostly ignores "isolinux"

add_entry creates distro objects based on:
    "kernel_options"
    "kernel_options_post"